{"availability":"available","full":"janpfeifer/gonb","name":"gonb","description":"GoNB, a Go Notebook Kernel for Jupyter","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":1050,"forks":56,"created":"2023-02-09T18:17:42Z","updated":"2026-07-27T08:43:38Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://github.com/janpfeifer/gonb","topics":["data-science","go","golang","gonb","jupyter","jupyter-notebook","jupyter-notebook-kernel"],"demo":"https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1vUd3SSoOm2K6UQLnkJQursZZx4CaIT_1?usp=sharing","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:31.428Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:31.428Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:31.428Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:31.428Z","stars":1050,"forks":56}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Go is a compiled language, but with very fast compilation, that allows one to use it in a REPL (Read-Eval-Print-Loop) fashion, by inserting a \"Compile\" step in the middle of the loop -- so it's a Read-Compile-Run-Print-Loop — while still feeling very interactive.","GoNB leverages that compilation speed to implement a full-featured (at least it's getting there) Jupyter notebook kernel. As a side benefit it works with packages that use CGO — although it won't parse C code in the cells, so it can't be used as a C kernel.","It already includes many goodies: cache between cell of results, contextual help and auto-complete (with gopls), compilation error context (by mousing over), bash command execution, images, html, etc. See the tutorial."],"features":["🚀 NEW 🚀: Windows (not WSL) support is working! Thanks to @StarWindv. (It's fresh from the oven, so there may be some kinks -- please report any issues!).","Auto-complete and contextual help while coding.","Rich content display: HTML, markdown (with latex), images, javascript, svg, videos, etc.","Widgets (sliders, buttons) support: interact using HTML elements. Create your own widgets!","Plotly integ